{{Quote|Welcome to Yavin 4....There are cells gathered here from every corner of the galaxy.|Garazeb Orrelios|<ref name="ITNOTR">{{Rebels|In the Name of the Rebellion}}</ref>}}
'''Yavin 4''',<ref name="DByav4" /> also known as '''Yavin''',<ref name="SWCT">{{SWCT|set=Base Series 1|cardname=Jan Dodonna - Rebel General}}</ref> was the [[jungle]]-covered fourth [[moon]] in orbit around the [[Color|red]] [[gas giant]] [[Yavin Prime]]. [[Early rebellion against the Galactic Empire|Prior to]] the [[Galactic Civil War]], Yavin was first a secret rendezvous point for members of the [[Axis network|Axis Network]]<ref name="Sagrona Teema">{{Andor|Sagrona Teema}}</ref> and later home to the [[Massassi Group]],<ref name="In the Name of the Rebellion">{{Rebels|In the Name of the Rebellion}}</ref> one of many disparate rebel cells fighting against the [[Galactic Empire]]. Sometime before [[2 BBY]], the [[Great Temple|headquarters]] of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]], was established on the moon,<ref name="Welcome to the Rebellion">{{Andor|Welcome to the Rebellion}}</ref> becoming fully equipped to wage war by [[1 BBY]].<ref name="Who Else Knows?">{{Andor|Who Else Knows?}}</ref> Following a [[Battle of Yavin|major battle]] that took place around Yavin,<ref name="ANH" /> the Alliance went on the run, and eventually [[Echo Base|relocated]] its headquarters to [[Hoth]].<ref name="ESB">{{Film|V}}</ref>

During the [[New Republic]] [[New Republic Era|Era]], [[Wetyin's Colony]] was the main settlement on the moon, and the [[Dameron family]] was [[Dameron homestead|settled]] there.<ref name="Shattered Empire 4" /> Due to New Republic [[Military Disarmament Act|demilitarization]], the [[Civilian Defense Force]] was founded to defend the moon. The Defense Force, along with the [[New Republic Security Bureau]], was later involved in an altercation with the [[Spice Runners of Kijimi]] after they crash-landed on the moon and escaped.<ref name="Free Fall" />

==Description==
The surface of Yavin 4 was divided into several continental masses, two of which were [[Starloft]] and [[Wetyin]].<ref name="ROUVG">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref> Notable natural formations included [[Massassi Valley]], [[Skygazer Hill]], and the [[Ferra Groves]].<ref name="Commander" /> The verdant world had a comfortable, [[Temperature|temperate]] climate but a challenging ecosystem and dangerous [[Diet|predators]].<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref>

The moon's landmasses were covered by dense [[jungle]]s and [[Forest|rain forests]], whose [[Plant|flora]] included [[Color|purple]]-barked [[Massassi tree]]s, [[grenade fungi]], [[Bioluminescence|bioluminescent]] [[orchid]]s, and [[climbing fern]]s. Yavin 4 also had [[swamp]]y areas.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars" /> The moon, however, was completely lacking in any [[mineral]] resources of significance.<ref name="Ultimate Star Wars New Edition">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref>

==History==
===Early history===
{{Quote|I know that the Massassi have been extinct for millennia. I knew that ''before'' I studied history.|Chelli Lona Aphra|<ref name="Doctor Aphra 3">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 3|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 3]]</ref>}}
[[File:Temple_of_Exar_Kun.jpg|thumb|left|250px|An ancient Massassi temple on Yavin 4.]]
[[5000 BBY|Five thousand]] [[Standard year|years]] before the [[Battle of Yavin]], the ancient [[Massassi warrior|warriors]] of the [[Massassi]] lived on Yavin 4 and constructed the [[Great Temple]].<ref name=":0">[[Star Wars: Journey Through Space (2015)|''Star Wars: Journey Through Space'']]</ref> The Great Temple was alleged to have been built under the leadership of the [[Sith Lord]] [[Naga Sadow]] around [[5000 BBY]].<ref name="BMF 23 Note">{{BuildFalconCite|23|Guide to the Galaxy}} establishes that the [[Great Temple]] on Yavin 4 was built by [[Massassi warrior]]s, allegedly under the leadership of Naga Sadow, around the [[Standard year|year]] [[5000 BBY]].</ref> The Massassi venerated the tyrant as a [[Deity|god]] and the Temple was raised in Sadow's honor. [[Archaeology|Archeologists]] later proposed that the Great Temple may have functioned as a large-scale [[Communications array|communications device]] to contact other Sith Lords throughout the [[galaxy]].<ref name="BMF 23">{{BuildFalconCite|23|Guide to the Galaxy}}</ref> Being [[Slavery|enslaved]] by the [[Sith]], the Massassi [[species]] went extinct<ref name="HC 76" /> [[Millennium|millennia]]<ref name="Doctor Aphra 3" /> before [[0 ABY]],<ref name="Aphra 3 Date">{{Aphra2016Date|3}}</ref> sometime after finishing their temples.<ref name="HC 76" />

Sometime before the [[Battle of Coruscant]], an [[Archaeology|archaeological]] [[Archaeological dig on Yavin 4|expedition]] on the moon of Yavin 4 uncovered the [[Great Sith Wars Bas-Relief]]<ref name="Coruscant">{{EncyclopediaCite|Coruscant}}</ref> in one of the enormous stone temples built by the Massassi.<ref name="HC 76" />

===Early rebellion===
By the [[Imperial Era]], Yavin 4 was only known to scouts and gas prospectors.<ref name="Galactic Explorer's Guide" /> In [[4 BBY]], [[Axis network]] agents, [[Cassian Andor]] and [[Porko]], chose Yavin 4 as their rendezvous point for after Andor's [[Theft of the TIE Avenger prototype|mission]] to [[Sienar Test Facility 73]]. However, a day after Andor left, the remnants of the [[Maya Pei Brigade]] arrived at Porko's location, and killed him when he opened fire on them. Andor would later return to the rendezvous point with the stolen [[TIE Avenger prototype]] two days later and was taken prisoner by the Brigade.<ref name="One Year Later">{{Andor|One Year Later}}</ref> Soon after, tensions among the Brigade boiled over and splintered into two sub-factions under [[Bardi]] and [[Gerdis]], the former holding the TIE Avenger while the latter holding Andor, the only pilot, hostage. The following night, Bardi and Gerdis resolved to settle their standoff with [[Five Hands]], only to be interrupted and devoured by a [[Yavinian doodar]]. Andor managed to escape in the chaos and retook the TIE Avenger and departed the moon, leaving the remaining rebels stranded.<ref name="Sagrona">{{Andor|Sagrona Teema}}</ref>

===Galactic Civil War===
{{Quote|&hellip;the Empire now knows our location. Therefore, our first priority is to find a new base of operations. To that end, all Rebel fleets have arrived to assist us in evacuating Yavin immediately.|Jan Dodonna|<ref name="Leia 1" />}}
[[File:Acme-DawnofRebellion.png|thumb|right|300px|The Great Temple was turned into a rebel base during the Galactic Civil War]]
By [[2 BBY]], the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] would utilize the temple during the [[Galactic Civil War]] as a base of operations against the then-dominant [[Galactic Empire]]. It was from this base that [[Operation Fracture]] was dispatched to [[Jedha]] in [[1 BBY]].<ref name="Rogue One">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> Shortly following this, Alliance [[Snub-fighter|snub fighter]] squadrons with orders to destroy the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] were also launched from Yavin 4. After the space battle and the related [[Royal Award Ceremony|award ceremony]], the rebels [[Evacuation of Yavin 4|evacuated]] the base to escape any retaliatory strike by the Empire.<ref name="ANH" /><ref name="Leia 1">[[Princess Leia 1|''Princess Leia'' 1]]</ref>

After the temple was abandoned by the rebels, a [[Unidentified Special Galaxy Reporter|Special Galaxy Reporter]] was sent to Yavin 4 to write a [[Tour the Great Temple on Yavin 4|travel advertisement]] about the ruins.<ref name=":0" /> The moon was also occupied by the Empire after the rebels fled, with Imperial walkers and [[stormtrooper]]s stationed around the former base. Amid the Imperial occupation, [[Doctor]] [[Korin Aphra]] led his daughter, [[Chelli Lona Aphra]], [[droid]]s [[0-0-0]] and [[BT-1]], and the [[Wookiee]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Krrsantan]] into a [[raid at the Great Temple]] during his search for the [[Ordu Aspectu]].<ref name="Doctor Aphra 2016 2" />

At another point, a rebel force was sent to the [[moon]] in order to seize leftover data centers from the previous rebel occupation. However, the Empire managed to discover the plot and also sent [[Imperial Military|forces]] to secure them for its own purposes. In the [[time]] before the [[Battle of Hoth]], multiple battles between Alliance and Imperial forces would occur on the moon's surface.<ref name="Commander" />

===New Republic Era===
{{Quote|Let's go ''home'', Shara Bey.|Kes Dameron|<ref name="Shattered Empire 4" />}}
[[File:SharaAndKesYavin4-ShatteredEmpire4.png|thumb|left|250px|Yavin 4 was home to the Dameron family during the New Republic Era]]
Around six [[Standard month|months]] after the [[Battle of Endor]] and after leaving the rebellion, [[Shara Bey]] and [[Kes Dameron]] [[Dameron homestead|settled down]] on Yavin 4 and planted the twig of a [[Great Tree (Coruscant)|Force-sensitive tree]] on the moon.<ref name="Before the Awakening">''[[Before the Awakening]]''</ref> During the [[New Republic Era]], the [[Civilian Defense Force]] or CDF was established to protect the moon after the [[New Republic]]'s [[New Republic Defense Fleet|Defense Fleet]] was [[Military Disarmament Act|reduced]], and Bey was a pilot in the Defense Force.<ref name="Free Fall" />

Future [[Resistance]] [[pilot]] [[Poe Dameron]] grew up on Yavin 4. While flying [[Shara Bey's A-wing|his mother's starfighter]], Poe was shot down by the CDF, which lead to a conflict with his [[Parent|father]] and close family-friend [[L'ulo L'ampar]]. Shortly after this, Poe ran away to [[Gully's]] cantina and joined the [[Spice Runners of Kijimi]], who had crashed on the moon. Flying their [[freighter]], the ''[[Ragged Claw]]'', Poe helped the Spice Runners narrowly escape the [[New Republic Security Bureau]], who had taken interest in the Spice Runners.<ref name="Free Fall" />

During the [[New Republic Era]], Yavin 4 was home to some settlers, as well as scavengers who would prowl the Death Star debris still in orbit. Although rare, tourists would occasionally visit the moon. The flora and fauna were of interest to nature enthusiasts.<ref name="Galactic Explorer's Guide" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:Yavin4BaseBriefingRoom-REBELION.png|thumb|right|250px|The council room set utilised  to convey one room of the Great Temple's interior, for episodes of ''Star Wars: Andor'''s second season.]]
Yavin 4 first appeared in the [[1977]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']], the first installment of the ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[original trilogy]].<ref name="ANH" />

The real-world location of Yavin 4 is the ruins of an ancient [[Wikipedia:Maya city|Mayan city]] at [[Tikal]], [[Wikipedia:Guatemala|Guatemala]]. Most of the shots of approaches to Yavin 4 from space are just repeats or copies of the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'' approach in ''A New Hope'', the only change being a ship replacement.

Yavin 4 is erroneously listed as a planet in the [[2016]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''.<ref name="VE" />

